473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (By combining efficient deep learning, and edge computing, this framework demonstrates that accurate diabetic retinopathy screening is no longer confined to specialised hospitals. It brings real-time diagnosis closer to underserved communities, making early detection more accessible and reducing the risk of preventable vision loss through timely clinical intervention.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Equally important is the system's ability to explain its decisions. Clinicians are understandably hesitant to trust a model that simply outputs a disease label without justification. To improve transparency and support clinical decision-making, the framework incorporates Gradient-weighted Class Activation Mapping \(Grad-CAM\), generating heat maps that highlight the retinal regions most responsible for each prediction. Areas containing microaneurysms, retinal haemorrhages, hard exudates, cotton-wool spots, or abnormal neovascularisation are visually emphasised and overlaid directly on the original fundus photograph. These explanations are generated in real time on the same Jetson Nano device, allowing healthcare professionals to verify the AI's reasoning rather than treating it as a black box. By combining efficient edge computing with explainable artificial intelligence, the system offers a practical and trustworthy solution for early diabetic retinopathy screening in underserved communities.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
