<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 158 0 R
/T (under the guidance of Dr. Prem Sankar Sir, Head of the Department, Providence College of Engineering. In CrowdVote AI, users can select constituencies and predict which political front is most likely to win. Instead of simple polling, the platform assigns a score called Signal Strength to each prediction. The score depends on two factors: the confidence level of the user and the timing of the prediction during different election phases. Predictions made with higher confidence receive greater weight in the final analysis.)
/E (under the guidance of Dr. Prem Sankar Sir, Head of the Department, Providence College of Engineering. In CrowdVote AI, users can select constituencies and predict which political front is most likely to win. Instead of simple polling, the platform assigns a score called Signal Strength to each prediction. The score depends on two factors: the confidence level of the user and the timing of the prediction during different election phases. Predictions made with higher confidence receive greater weight in the final analysis.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
