656 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 166 0 R
/T (Type 1 Diabetes is an autoimmune disease in which the body's immunesystem attacks and destroys insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas. As a result, the body produces little to no insulin, causing glucose to build up in the blood instead of entering cells for energy. Though the exact cause is not fully understood, it is believed to involve genetic and environmental factors. Symptoms often appear suddenly excessive thirst, frequent urination, fatigue, weight loss, and blurred vision and without proper care, it can lead to serious long-term complications. )
/E (Type 1 Diabetes is an autoimmune disease in which the body's immunesystem attacks and destroys insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas. As a result, the body produces little to no insulin, causing glucose to build up in the blood instead of entering cells for energy. Though the exact cause is not fully understood, it is believed to involve genetic and environmental factors. Symptoms often appear suddenly excessive thirst, frequent urination, fatigue, weight loss, and blurred vision and without proper care, it can lead to serious long-term complications. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
