/Title (At the age of 12, my life took an unexpected turn when I was diagnosed with Type 1 Diabetes. Now, at 19, I have spent eight years learning not just how to manage it, but how to live alongside it. Type 1 Diabetes is a lifelong condition that demands constant attention, discipline, and resilience. Every day involves careful decisions about food, insulin, activity, and rest, shaping me into someone more aware, responsible, and strong.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2990 0 R
/Next 3209 0 R
>>
endobj
3172 0 obj
<<
/Title (Type 1 Diabetes is an autoimmune disease in which the body's immunesystem attacks and destroys insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas. As a result, the body produces little to no insulin, causing glucose to build up in the blood instead of entering cells for energy. Though the exact cause is not fully understood, it is believed to involve genetic and environmental factors. Symptoms often appear suddenly excessive thirst, frequent urination, fatigue, weight loss, and blurred vision and without proper care, it can lead to serious long-term complications.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2990 0 R
/Prev 3209 0 R
>>
